  "documentation" : {
    "decisions" : [ {
      "content" : "# 1. Record architecture decisions\n\nDate: 2025-09-19\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nWe need to record the architectural decisions made on this project.\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will use Architecture Decision Records, as [described by Michael Nygard](http://thinkrelevance.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions).\n\n## Consequences\n\nSee Michael Nygard's article, linked above. For a lightweight ADR toolset, see Nat Pryce's [adr-tools](https://github.com/npryce/adr-tools).\n",
      "date" : "2025-09-19T00:00:00Z",
      "format" : "Markdown",
      "id" : "1",
      "status" : "Accepted",
      "title" : "Record architecture decisions"
    }, {
      "content" : "# 2. Use C4 diagrams\n\nDate: 2025-09-19\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nI need to get used to using C4.\n\n## Decision\n\nDraw diagrams for my R package for analyzing my running data\ndownloaded from Strava.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- My programming style will become more organized, I hope.\n",
      "date" : "2025-09-19T00:00:00Z",
      "format" : "Markdown",
      "id" : "2",
      "status" : "Accepted",
      "title" : "Use C4 diagrams"
    }, {
      "content" : "# 3. User interacts with system through a menu\n\nDate: 2025-09-19\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nAlthough reports will be the main output of the system, we do not want\nthe user to have to open, edit and execute the qmd files.\n\n## Decision\n\nBase interaction on a main menu, possibly with submenus. Implement a\ncontroller for this.\n\n## Consequences\n\nIt becomes clearer what the actions are.\n",
      "date" : "2025-09-19T00:00:00Z",
      "format" : "Markdown",
      "id" : "3",
      "status" : "Accepted",
      "title" : "User interacts with system through a menu"
    }, {
      "content" : "# 4. Use marimo for interactive reports\n\nDate: 2025-09-20\n\n## Status\n\nPending\n\n## Context\n\nI need to decide how to present information (tables, plots) to the user.\n\n## Decision\n\nUse marimo notebooks to show interactive plots. Or use quarto + marimo.\n\n## Consequences\n\nI will learn how to use marimo. \n",
      "date" : "2025-09-20T00:00:00Z",
      "format" : "Markdown",
      "id" : "4",
      "status" : "Pending",
      "title" : "Use marimo for interactive reports"
    } ],
